  "title": "Lee2021 – SSVEP paradigm of the Mobile BCI dataset",
  "description": "This dataset contains the steady-state visual evoked potential (SSVEP) paradigm of the Mobile BCI dataset from Lee et al. (2021). It provides scalp EEG and EOG recordings from healthy participants who viewed visual flickers at 5.45, 8.57, and 12 Hz while standing, walking, and running on a treadmill. It supports research on brain-computer interface decoding during locomotion.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BrainAmp amplifier (Brain Products) using Ag/AgCl electrodes, with FCz as reference and Fpz as ground. The montage was standard_1005 with 73 EEG channels plus 4 EOG channels. Participants performed 5 s trials of a three-class SSVEP task across multiple sessions. Impedance was kept below 50 kOhm. Reported classifiers were rLDA and CCA.",
